# Solve-ent commits to `staging`. `main` is production: it is the Cloudflare
# Pages production branch, so a commit landing there is a commit landing on the
# address a class opens. Promotion is a merge, said out loud.
work=staging
promote=main
escape=SOLVENT_PROMOTE

# Run on EVERY commit, including a promote, because it is about what is being
# committed rather than where. The release triplet is one number in several
# places, and the failure mode is a build reporting a version its code is not —
# which sends the next screenshot after a defect that was fixed two releases ago.
also=tools/version-check.mjs

# AND THE WORDS, on every commit, because this is the rule a later session
# undoes in one well-meaning commit. Adding a streak counter is an afternoon's
# work and feels like kindness; it teaches a student to chase the animation and
# makes stopping feel like failing, which is exactly wrong for the person who
# most needs to do twenty of these. Same for copy that assumes a classroom a
# homeschooler does not have.
also=tools/copy-check.mjs

# And the release notes, which are GENERATED from CHANGELOG.md and committed.
# A generated artefact in the tree is a generated artefact that goes stale in
# the tree — and a what's-new panel one release behind is a panel telling
# somebody about a change they do not have.
also=tools/notes-check.mjs

# And the hub pin, which is the same commit written in two files: the marker
# `doctrine-sync --adopt` moves, and the SHA CI checks the hub out at to run the
# shared gates. Adopting is one command and editing a workflow is another, and
# skipping the second leaves CI enforcing rules from before the ones this repo
# has already read — every gate green, the new rule enforced nowhere.
also=tools/hub-pin-check.mjs

# The colour tokens, which are GENERATED from palettes/solve-ent.json — the file
# the hub's palette gate measures. Two declarations of one colour means the
# values that were measured and the values a browser paints can differ, which is
# the drift factory PALETTES.md says to close before there is more than one of
# anything.
also=tools/palette-check.mjs

# The engine as a browser runs it, which lives in public/ because public/ IS the
# site. That makes staleness the risk rather than a missing build, and this is
# the gate for it.
also=tools/web-check.mjs

# And that every source file is in SOME TypeScript project. `exclude` is
# inherited through `extends`, which is how the whole browser layer came to be
# checked by neither config while both exited 0.
also=tools/coverage-check.mjs

# The icons, GENERATED from palettes/solve-ent.json. An icon is the one surface
# the accessibility gate cannot reach — it is not in the document, so nothing
# reverse-maps its colours to a token and nothing measures its contrast. That
# makes it the easiest place in the application for an unmeasured colour to
# appear and stay, so the colours are read from the file the palette gate
# measures rather than typed beside it.
also=tools/icon-check.mjs

# The service worker and the manifest, GENERATED from the version and the tree.
# The cache name has to move with the release or everyone who already has the app
# keeps the old shell forever — and the app cannot notice, which is what caching
# means. The precache list has to be what public/ actually contains, or a module
# is silently not there offline.
also=tools/pwa-check.mjs
